# tv_menu_headless: the TV in-game menu and its input ownership, through the real App (headless, no ImGui).
# Run with:  virtualjaguar --headless --frames 30 --tv-test-script tv_menu_headless.txt
# (VJ_LIBRASHADER must point at a missing path when this script is run by hand, as cmake/VJTvTests.cmake sets it for ctest: a
# shader runtime would add a Picture row and the Down counts below would be off.)
# One event per line:  <ms> <verb> <args>.  <ms> is a script time; the gap to the previous line is the least real time
# that passes between the two (the hold arbiter reads the real clock).  Lines starting with # are comments.
#   load PATH            drop PATH on the window (the normal drop route)
#   key down|up|tap NAME a key event (SDL scancode name: F4, Escape, F8; "ctrl+L", "ctrl+shift+T" = with those held)
#   pad down|up|tap BTN  a button on the runner's virtual gamepad (SDL button name: a, b, dpdown, misc1)
#   mouse X Y           move the pointer to X,Y in the main window: a MOUSE_MOTION with the travel since the last `mouse` line as xrel / yrel
#                       (windowed: the real pointer is warped there too, for hover tests; headless: only the event)
#   expect fullscreen=0|1 menu-pinned=0|1 menu-visible=0|1 (menu-visible needs a windowed rendered frame)
#   focus lost|gained    the window loses / gets keyboard focus
#   typing on|off        pretend a text box has focus (input.uiWantsKeyboard)
#   capture help|tvmenu  begin binding that action on the keyboard (the next key becomes its binding)
#   capture nav:INTENT   begin rebinding a menu button of the virtual pad (confirm back menu favorite start tabprev tabnext pageprev
#                        pagenext search): the next pad button becomes it (#1021).  expect cfg=...{padguid}... is its GUID.
#   tvsetting off|manual|auto  set the stored TV-mode setting and reconfigure (as Settings will); off = never, auto = also in fullscreen and on a pad press
#   fullscreen on|off    enter / leave fullscreen (headless: the flag and the edge TV mode is told about, no window)
#   hintreset            forget the one-time TV mode hint (ui.tv_hint_shown and this run's flag) and zero toast-count
#   expect toast=TEXT    the text of the last toast (the rest of the line, spaces included);  expect toast-count=N  toasts shown since start
#   expect tv-setting=off|manual|auto  the stored setting (a fresh config takes the build default: auto on a CTest build)
#   navdefault INTENT    the Default button of that menu intent of the virtual pad (back to the family's button, partner swapped back)
#   expect menu-open=0|1  paused=0|1  loaded=0|1  capturing=0|1  fast-forward=0|1  core-input=0|1  kb-bind=help|tvmenu:KEY
#   expect tv=0|1         TV mode is on
#   expect tv-screen=ID   the id of the TV screen on top (home, library, ...)
#   expect tv-focus=LABEL the label of what has the focus on the top TV screen (Settings: the group on the rail, or the row in its list;
#                         the rest of the line, spaces included); Screen::focusLabel()
#   expect tv-owns-input=0|1  the TV shell has the pads and keys (0 while a desktop window covers the TV screens)
#   expect settings-open=0|1  the desktop Settings window is open
#   expect tv-more=0|1        it was opened by "More settings..." in TV mode: the pads and the arrow keys are its own (tv_more_settings.h)
#   expect home-visible=0|1   the desktop library is standing in for the game (never while TV mode is on)
#   expect library-window=0|1 the desktop Game library window is open
#   expect desk-pad=0|1       the desktop library owns the pads (#1021): TV off, no game running, no capture / desktop window, no mouse-opened popup
#                             (headless has no ImGui context, so that last part is covered by tv_ui_smoke)
#   axis NAME VALUE       set an axis of the virtual pad (SDL axis name: righty, lefttrigger; -32768..32767)
#   expect desk-scroll=0|1    the desktop nav holds a right-stick scroll (nonzero)
#   expect desk-pending=N     commands the desktop nav has queued (headless nothing draws the library, so they stay queued)
#   expect desk-popup=0|1     a library popup (tile menu, BIOS popup) opened from the pad is open and driven by it
#   saveconfig           App::saveConfig() (a headless run keeps its config in a private temp dir)
#   expect cfg=KEY:VALUE  the config holds KEY = VALUE; KEY:absent = the config has no such key
#   expect core-option=KEY:VALUE  the core option KEY reads VALUE (a session override, else the saved value: CoreHost::optionValueFor)
#   wait library         WINDOWED ONLY: block the script until the Library has scanned (not scanning, and at least one
#                        game); FAIL after 120 s.  The gaps of the lines after it count from the moment it is released.
#   shot PATH            WINDOWED ONLY: save the window as a PNG at the end of the next UI frame (that frame's TV drawing
#                        included).  Leave a gap before it for a screen change to finish animating.
#   quit                 WINDOWED ONLY: end the run through the normal teardown
#   (headless, wait / shot / quit fail their line with "windowed only": the Library is scanned by threads that only a
#   windowed run starts, and there is no window to save.  Windowed, any FAIL is printed and the script goes on.)
#   (core-input=1: the core would read some Player 1 pad button right now; the expect takes the snapshot itself)
# An expect first lets the per-frame input housekeeping run, so a fired hold has been handled by then.

# TV mode with no game (Manual): F4 turns it on and off; Esc at the root is not the shell's; Off ignores F4; the toggle works under
# Auto too; a Share hold toggles it too.  (A fresh config takes the build default, Auto on a CTest build: start from Manual.)
0     tvsetting manual
0     expect loaded=0
0     expect tv=0
0     key tap F4
40    expect tv=1
40    expect tv-screen=home
60    key tap Escape          # at root: not the shell's
100   expect tv=1
100   key tap F4
140   expect tv=0
140   tvsetting off
160   key tap F4
200   expect tv=0
200   tvsetting auto           # the toggle works under Auto too
220   key tap F4
260   expect tv=1
260   key tap F4
300   expect tv=0
300   tvsetting manual
320   pad down misc1
920   pad up misc1
960   expect tv=1
960   key tap F4
1000  expect tv=0

# saveConfig() never writes ui.tv_mode (a stored value would pin a default that moves between builds); only a change in Settings
# does.  The remembered on/off state (ui.tv_manual_on) is written under Manual.  Whatever the setting, the key stays out of the config.
1000  tvsetting manual
1000  saveconfig
1000  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:absent
1000  key tap F4
1040  expect tv=1
1040  saveconfig
1040  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:absent
1040  expect cfg=ui.tv_manual_on:1
1040  key tap F4
1080  expect tv=0
1080  saveconfig
1080  expect cfg=ui.tv_manual_on:0
1080  tvsetting auto
1080  saveconfig
1080  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:absent
1080  tvsetting manual

# With TV mode on, Ctrl+L (File > Game library) opens the desktop library WINDOW (the home library is not showing: the TV
# screens stand in for it); with it off the home library is showing, so Ctrl+L only focuses its search box.  While the window
# covers the TV screens they take no pad input (RB would step to the Library section), and they get it back when it closes.
1080  expect home-visible=1
1080  key tap ctrl+L
1120  expect library-window=0
1120  key tap F4
1160  expect tv=1
1160  expect home-visible=0
1160  expect tv-owns-input=1
1160  key tap ctrl+L
1200  expect library-window=1
1200  expect tv-owns-input=0
1200  pad tap rightshoulder
1240  expect tv-screen=home
1240  key tap ctrl+L
1280  expect library-window=0
1280  expect tv-owns-input=1
1280  pad tap rightshoulder
1320  expect tv-screen=library
1320  pad tap leftshoulder
1360  expect tv-screen=home
1360  key tap F4
1400  expect tv=0

# "More settings..." from TV mode (#991): A on the last row of Interface opens the desktop Settings window and hands it the pad.
# RB x3 reaches Settings (Home, Library, Achievements, Settings).  With no game this session the core rows are hidden and Speed
# holds only its "Available once a game has run" line, so the rail is Picture, Speed, Sound, Interface (Down x3); Right enters the list: Show FPS, VSync, Theme, TV mode, More settings... (Down x4).
# While the window is open the shell has stepped aside (tv-owns-input=0) and the pad is the window's: a shoulder button that
# would change section does nothing, and B closes it (no popup, no active item), giving the pad back.
1400  key tap F4
1440  expect tv=1
1440  pad tap rightshoulder
1460  pad tap rightshoulder
1480  pad tap rightshoulder
1500  expect tv-screen=settings
1500  pad tap dpdown
1510  pad tap dpdown
1520  pad tap dpdown
1540  pad tap dpright
1560  pad tap dpdown
1580  pad tap dpdown
1600  pad tap dpdown
1620  pad tap dpdown
1640  pad tap a
1680  expect settings-open=1
1680  expect tv-more=1
1680  expect tv-owns-input=0
1680  pad tap dpdown              # the window's, not the shell's
1700  pad tap leftshoulder        # would step back to Achievements
1720  expect tv-screen=settings
1720  pad tap b
1760  expect settings-open=0
1760  expect tv-more=0
1760  expect tv-owns-input=1
# Esc closes it too (the focus is still on More settings...), and so does Ctrl+, -- which also ends the TV hand-off: the next
# Ctrl+, opens the plain desktop window.
1760  pad tap a
1800  expect tv-more=1
1800  key tap Escape
1840  expect settings-open=0
1840  expect tv-more=0
1840  pad tap a
1880  expect tv-more=1
1880  key tap ctrl+,
1920  expect settings-open=0
1920  expect tv-more=0
1920  key tap ctrl+,
1960  expect settings-open=1
1960  expect tv-more=0
1960  key tap ctrl+,
2000  expect settings-open=0
2000  pad tap leftshoulder        # back to Home (the shell remembers the section across TV mode off / on)
2010  pad tap leftshoulder
2020  pad tap leftshoulder
2040  expect tv-screen=home
2040  key tap F4
2080  expect tv=0

# Desktop pad navigation (#1021): the desktop library owns the pads while TV mode is off, no game is running and the home
# library shows.  A shoulder button is a mapped intent (SectionNext = next tab) and queues a command; TV mode on (or an edge of
# any ownership input) hands the pad to the TV screens and clears what was queued.
2080  expect desk-pad=1
2080  expect cfg=ui.tv_hint_shown:absent
2080  expect toast-count=0
2080  pad tap rightshoulder
# The first consumed press under Manual shows the one-time hint (6 s toast, wording from the pad's own TV-menu binding: the virtual
# pad has Share, so its default is the Share hold), stored before it shows; a second press shows nothing more.
2120  expect toast=Press Share (hold) or F4 for TV mode
2120  expect cfg=ui.tv_hint_shown:1
2120  expect toast-count=1
2120  expect desk-pending=1
2120  pad tap leftshoulder
2160  expect toast-count=1
2160  expect desk-pending=2
2160  key tap F4
2200  expect tv=1
2200  expect desk-pad=0
2200  expect desk-pending=0      # the edge cleared the queue
2200  pad tap leftshoulder        # TV's, not the desktop library's: nothing queues
2240  expect desk-pending=0
2240  key tap F4
2280  expect tv=0
2280  expect desk-pad=1
# A binding capture owns the pad.
2280  capture help
2320  expect capturing=1
2320  expect desk-pad=0
2320  key tap Return             # ends the capture
2360  expect capturing=0
2360  expect desk-pad=1
# Start (Menu) is not the library's: it stays the app's and queues nothing.
2360  pad tap start
2400  expect desk-pending=0

# A right stick pushed while the library listens is a scroll; losing the pad (a desktop window opens, Settings here) or the
# window's focus zeroes it, so a stick let go meanwhile cannot scroll on.  Settings takes the pad while open.
2440  axis righty 30000
2480  expect desk-scroll=1
2480  key tap ctrl+,
2520  expect desk-pad=0
2520  expect desk-scroll=0
2520  axis righty 0
2560  key tap ctrl+,
2600  expect desk-pad=1
2600  expect desk-scroll=0
2600  axis righty 30000
2640  expect desk-scroll=1
2640  focus lost
2680  expect desk-scroll=0
2680  axis righty 0
2720  expect desk-scroll=0

# Auto (#991 phase 4): a mapped pad press in the desktop library turns TV mode on and is consumed (nothing queued, nothing
# launched); a printable key turns a controller-started TV mode off; fullscreen holds it; leaving fullscreen ends it.
2760  tvsetting auto
2760  expect tv=0
2760  expect desk-pad=1
2760  pad tap a
2800  expect tv=1
2800  expect tv-screen=home
2800  expect loaded=0
2800  expect desk-pending=0
2800  expect toast-count=1            # no second hint (and the switching press takes the return before the hint site)
2800  key tap Escape               # approval C: Esc, Enter and shortcuts are not "typing": a controller-started TV mode stays on
2800  expect tv=1
2800  key tap Return
2800  expect tv=1
2800  key tap ctrl+H               # a printable key with Ctrl held is a shortcut
2800  expect tv=1
2800  key tap H
2840  expect tv=0
2840  pad tap dpdown
2880  expect tv=1
2880  fullscreen on
2900  expect fullscreen=1
2900  key tap H
2940  expect tv=1                 # fullscreen holds it
2940  fullscreen off
2980  expect tv=0
2980  fullscreen on
3020  expect tv=1                 # the fullscreen trigger on its own
3020  key tap ctrl+shift+T
3060  expect tv=0                 # manual wins ...
3060  key tap H
3100  expect tv=0
3100  fullscreen off
3100  fullscreen on
3140  expect tv=1                 # ... until the next edge
3140  fullscreen off
3180  expect tv=0
3180  pad tap touchpad            # no nav intent (C_HELP's button): not a trigger.  (Not misc1: a Share tap opens the keypad overlay)
3220  expect tv=0
3220  pad tap start
3260  expect tv=1                 # Start is a mapped intent: it switches
3260  key tap H
3300  expect tv=0
3300  key tap ctrl+,              # a desktop window takes the pad before the trigger sees it
3340  pad tap dpdown
3380  expect tv=0
3380  key tap ctrl+,
# A Share hold toggles TV mode (Manual cause) and is not also the controller trigger (it would switch on at the press, off at the hold).
3380  pad down misc1
4000  expect tv=1
4000  pad up misc1
4040  expect tv=1
4040  key tap F4
4080  expect tv=0
4080  tvsetting manual
4080  saveconfig
4080  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:absent

# The Auto rows in TV Settings (#991 phase 4): they exist only under Auto, a change is stored and keeps TV mode on (a reconfigure
# makes it a Manual-started one), and Auto -> Manual removes them.  Every step of the walk is anchored by `expect tv-focus=` (the
# group on the rail, the row in the list), because the shell remembers Settings across TV mode off and on and the Base layer resumes
# the level (list or rail) and the row it was left on: nothing here may assume where an earlier test stopped.  TV mode comes back on
# at Home.  RB x3 opens Settings at whatever level it was left; one Back then goes from the list to the groups, or from the groups
# to Home; LB x3 makes it Home either way, leaving the memory on the groups; RB x3 reopens Settings there.  Up x4 must read Picture
# and Down x3 Interface; only then does Right enter the list (on the groups it only enters, it changes nothing).  Up x8 clamps to
# Show FPS, Down x4 must read Auto: in fullscreen, and only then do Left / Right change a value.
# With Auto on the list is Show FPS, VSync, Theme, TV mode, Auto: in fullscreen, Auto: when a controller is used, More settings...
4080  tvsetting auto
4090  key tap F4
4130  expect tv=1
4130  expect tv-screen=home
4140  pad tap rightshoulder
4150  pad tap rightshoulder
4160  pad tap rightshoulder
4200  expect tv-screen=settings
4210  pad tap b
4220  pad tap leftshoulder
4230  pad tap leftshoulder
4240  pad tap leftshoulder
4280  expect tv-screen=home
4290  pad tap rightshoulder
4300  pad tap rightshoulder
4310  pad tap rightshoulder
4350  expect tv-screen=settings
4360  pad tap dpup
4370  pad tap dpup
4380  pad tap dpup
4390  pad tap dpup
4430  expect tv-focus=Picture
4440  pad tap dpdown
4450  pad tap dpdown
4460  pad tap dpdown
4500  expect tv-focus=Interface
4510  pad tap dpright
4520  pad tap dpup
4530  pad tap dpup
4540  pad tap dpup
4550  pad tap dpup
4560  pad tap dpup
4570  pad tap dpup
4580  pad tap dpup
4590  pad tap dpup
4630  expect tv-focus=Show FPS
4640  pad tap dpdown
4650  pad tap dpdown
4660  pad tap dpdown
4670  pad tap dpdown
4710  expect tv-focus=Auto: in fullscreen
4710  pad tap dpleft
4750  expect cfg=ui.tv_auto_fullscreen:0
4750  expect tv=1   # still on (Manual cause after the reconfigure)
4760  pad tap dpright
4800  expect cfg=ui.tv_auto_fullscreen:1
4800  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:absent   # the checkbox change saved the config, and still did not pin the default
4810  pad tap dpup
4850  expect tv-focus=TV mode
4850  pad tap dpleft   # Auto -> Manual
4890  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:manual
4890  expect tv=1
4900  pad tap dpdown
4940  expect tv-focus=More settings…   # the Auto rows are gone
4940  pad tap a
4980  expect tv-more=1
4980  pad tap b
5020  expect tv-more=0
5030  pad tap leftshoulder   # back to Home: the shell resumes the screen TV mode was left on, and the lines below start from Home
5040  pad tap leftshoulder
5050  pad tap leftshoulder
5090  expect tv-screen=home
5090  key tap F4
5130  expect tv=0

# The hint never shows under Off or Auto, even with the key unset and the run's flag clear (hintreset: forget both, zero toast-count).
5130  hintreset
5130  tvsetting off
5130  expect desk-pad=1
5130  expect desk-pending=0
5140  pad tap rightshoulder
5160  expect desk-pending=1            # the desktop library took the press (so the hint site was reached) ...
5160  expect toast-count=0             # ... and showed nothing
5160  expect cfg=ui.tv_hint_shown:absent
5160  tvsetting auto
5160  mouse 100 100                  # (TV mode is off: the pointer's start is not travel)
5170  pad tap a                      # Auto's switching press: consumed, no hint
5180  expect tv=1
5180  expect toast-count=0
5180  expect cfg=ui.tv_hint_shown:absent
# The mouse path through App::handleEvent: 30 px of motion (3 x 10) leave a controller-started TV mode on, the 4th step (40 px) ends it.
# (A warp reports xrel = 0, so `mouse` also pushes the motion event itself; the windowed check on the Studio sends the same.)
5180  mouse 110 100
5180  mouse 120 100
5180  mouse 130 100
5185  expect tv=1
5185  mouse 140 100
5190  expect tv=0

# A game to play with.
5190  load @VJ_ROMS@/yarc.j64
5230  expect loaded=1

# Auto with a game running (#991 phase 4): a pad press is the game's, never a trigger; fullscreen still turns TV mode on and leaves
# the game running, unpaused, with its input; leaving fullscreen turns it off.
5230  tvsetting auto
5230  pad tap dpdown
5270  expect tv=0                 # the game owns the pad
5270  fullscreen on
5310  expect tv=1
5310  expect menu-open=0
5310  expect paused=0
5310  pad down dpright
5350  expect core-input=1
5350  pad up dpright
5350  fullscreen off
5390  expect tv=0
5390  tvsetting manual

# F4 opens the menu (and pauses the game), F4 again closes it.
5430   key tap F4
5470   expect menu-open=1
5470   expect paused=1
5490   key tap F4
5530   expect menu-open=0
5530   expect paused=0

# A pause the player made is theirs: the menu does not undo it.
5550   key tap F8
5570   expect paused=1
5590   key tap F4
5630   expect menu-open=1
5650   key tap F4
5690   expect menu-open=0
5690   expect paused=1
5710   key tap F8
5730   expect paused=0

# F4 while a text box has the keyboard does nothing.
5750   typing on
5770   key tap F4
5810   expect menu-open=0
5810   typing off

# Esc is Back, and Back on the menu's first page is Resume.
5830   key tap F4
5870   expect menu-open=1
5890   key tap Escape
5930   expect menu-open=0
5930   expect paused=0

# A key let go while the menu is open still reaches the app (Tab is fast-forward and has to be let go of).
5950   key down Tab
5970   expect fast-forward=1
5990   key tap F4
6030   expect menu-open=1
6050   key up Tab
6090   expect fast-forward=0
6110   key tap F4
6150   expect menu-open=0

# A Share tap is not a hold: no menu.
# (`pad tap` presses and releases inside one line, so a stalled runner cannot stretch it into a hold.)
6190   pad tap misc1
6270   expect menu-open=0

# A Share hold of 600 ms opens the menu; letting go leaves it open.
6290   pad down misc1
6910  expect menu-open=1
6910  expect paused=1
6930  pad up misc1
6970  expect menu-open=1

# A Share hold while it is open closes it (the edge reaches the arbiter before the shell).
6990  pad down misc1
7630  expect menu-open=0
7630  expect paused=0
7650  pad up misc1
7690  expect menu-open=0

# Focus lost 200 ms into a Share hold: the hold is forgotten, so 700 ms later the menu is still closed.
7710  pad down misc1
7910  focus lost
8610  expect menu-open=0
8610  pad up misc1
8650  expect menu-open=0

# The menu holds the pause: F8 under it is refused, and closing gives back the state from before the menu.
8670  key tap F4
8710  expect menu-open=1
8710  expect paused=1
8730  key tap F8
8770  expect paused=1
8770  expect menu-open=1
8790  key tap F4
8830  expect menu-open=0
8830  expect paused=0

# The menu owns the input: with it open the core reads neutral input (under netplay the menu cannot pause the game, and this is
# what keeps it from playing under the menu); a button held across the close stays masked until released; with the menu closed it plays.
8850  key tap F4
8890  expect menu-open=1
8910  pad down dpright
8950  expect core-input=0
8970  pad up dpright
8990  pad down dpright
9010  key tap F4
9050  expect menu-open=0
9050  expect core-input=0
9070  pad up dpright
9090  expect core-input=0
9110  pad down dpright
9150  expect core-input=1
9170  pad up dpright
9210  expect core-input=0

# F4 while a binding is being captured binds F4 and does not open the menu.
9230  capture help
9250  key tap F4
9290  expect capturing=0
9290  expect menu-open=0
9290  expect kb-bind=help:F4

# Walk the menu with the pad (nine rows down: Save state, Load state, Achievements, Overlays, Settings, Controls, the TV-mode row, Reset, Close game): ask, answer No (back to the menu), ask again, Up to Yes (focus starts on No), answer Yes.
9330  key tap F4
9370  expect menu-open=1
9390  pad tap dpdown
9400  pad tap dpdown
9410  pad tap dpdown
9420  pad tap dpdown
9430  pad tap dpdown
9440  pad tap dpdown
9450  pad tap dpdown
9470  pad tap dpdown
9480  pad tap dpdown
9490  pad tap a
9510  pad tap a
9550  expect menu-open=1
9550  expect loaded=1
9570  pad tap a
9590  pad tap dpup
9610  pad tap a
9650  expect loaded=0
9650  expect menu-open=0

# TV mode survives a game: turn it on, walk to Library, start a game (the TV screen goes away under it), close the game
# from the in-game menu -- and the TV screen the player left is back.
9730  key tap F4
9770  expect tv=1
9770  expect tv-screen=home
9790  pad tap rightshoulder
9830  expect tv-screen=library
9830  load @VJ_ROMS@/yarc.j64
9870  expect loaded=1
9870  expect tv=1
9890  key tap F4
9930  expect menu-open=1
9930  expect tv=1
9950  pad tap dpdown
9960  pad tap dpdown
9970  pad tap dpdown
9980  pad tap dpdown
9990  pad tap dpdown
10000  pad tap dpdown
10010  pad tap dpdown
10030  pad tap dpdown
10040  pad tap dpdown
10050  pad tap a
10070  pad tap dpup
10090  pad tap a
10130  expect loaded=0
10130  expect menu-open=0
10130  expect tv-screen=library
10150  key tap F4
10190  expect tv=0

# A binding capture started with TV mode on keeps its input: the shoulder button that would switch sections (the screen
# the player left is Library: LB would take it to Home) and the Return key that would be Accept go to the capture instead
# of navigating.
10230  key tap F4
10270  expect tv=1
10270  expect tv-screen=library
10290  capture help
10310  pad tap leftshoulder
10350  expect tv-screen=library
10370  key tap Return
10410  expect capturing=0
10410  expect tv-screen=library
10410  expect kb-bind=help:Return
10430  key tap F4
10470  expect tv=0

# Ctrl+Shift+T (Cmd+Shift+T on a Mac) toggles TV mode with or without a game, whatever F4 is bound to; a game keeps running
# and the in-game menu stays shut.  It is ignored while a text box has the keyboard or a binding is being captured, and does
# nothing when the TV-mode setting is Off.
10490  key tap ctrl+shift+T
10530  expect tv=1
10530  expect menu-open=0
10530  key tap ctrl+shift+T
10570  expect tv=0
10570  key tap ctrl+T
10610  expect tv=0                # Ctrl alone is not the shortcut
10610  key tap shift+T
10650  expect tv=0
10650  typing on
10670  key tap ctrl+shift+T
10710  expect tv=0
10710  typing off
10710  capture help
10730  key tap ctrl+shift+T
10770  expect tv=0
10770  key tap Return             # ends the capture, if the shortcut did not already
10810  expect capturing=0
10810  tvsetting off
10830  key tap ctrl+shift+T
10870  expect tv=0
10870  tvsetting manual

# With a game loaded: the shortcut turns TV mode on and off, the game stays loaded and running, no menu opens.
10890  load @VJ_ROMS@/yarc.j64
10930  expect loaded=1
10930  key tap ctrl+shift+T
10970  expect tv=1
10970  expect loaded=1
10970  expect menu-open=0
10970  expect paused=0
10970  key tap ctrl+shift+T
11010  expect tv=0
11010  expect loaded=1
11010  expect menu-open=0
11010  expect paused=0
11010  key tap F4              # F4 with a game is still the menu, not the TV-mode toggle
11050  expect menu-open=1
11050  expect tv=0
11050  key tap F4
11090  expect menu-open=0

# A running game owns its pad: the desktop library does not, whether or not its window is open.  Paused with the window open it
# does again.
11090  expect menu-open=0
11090  expect desk-pad=0
11090  key tap ctrl+L
11130  expect library-window=1
11130  expect desk-pad=0
11130  key tap F8
11170  expect paused=1
11170  expect desk-pad=1
11170  pad tap rightshoulder
11210  expect desk-pending=1
11210  key tap F8
11250  expect paused=0
11250  expect desk-pad=0
11250  key tap F8
11290  expect desk-pad=1
11290  key tap ctrl+L
11330  expect library-window=0
11330  expect desk-pad=0
11330  key tap F8
11370  expect paused=0

# Menu buttons (#1021): Set captures the virtual pad's next button for a menu intent, and writes no game binding.  North (Y)
# becomes Confirm; Y was Favorite's, so the two swap (Favorite takes Confirm's old button, South).
11370  expect capturing=0
11370  capture nav:confirm
11410  expect capturing=1
11410  pad tap y
11450  expect capturing=0
11450  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.confirm:by
11450  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.favorite:ba
# Default on one half of the swap puts both back: no two intents on one button, and no stray key.
11450  navdefault confirm
11490  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.confirm:absent
11490  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.favorite:absent
# A reserved button is refused and writes nothing: the D-pad moves, so it cannot be a menu button.
11490  capture nav:back
11530  pad tap dpup
11570  expect capturing=0
11570  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.back:absent
# So is the button that opens the controls overlay (the pad's C_HELP, the touchpad button), as the TV-menu button is.
11570  capture nav:back
11610  pad tap touchpad
11650  expect capturing=0
11650  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.back:absent
# Esc cancels a menu-button capture without writing anything.
11650  capture nav:search
11690  key tap Escape
11730  expect capturing=0
11730  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.search:absent

# A core option changed inside the in-game menu reaches the core once the menu is closed.  Down x5 from Resume is Settings (Save state,
# Load state, Achievements, Overlays, Settings), A opens the screen (the groups), Up x4 is Picture whatever group the Settings screen
# was left on earlier in the script (the shell remembers it), A opens Picture (the shader row is absent: the test rules the
# library out), Down x2 is Internal resolution (Integer scaling, Aspect ratio, then it), Right steps it from the core's
# default (1x) to 2x; B x3 is rows -> groups -> the menu -> Resume.  The write is a posted command: the value is read after the menu
# has closed and the paused core has had its boundary.
11770   load @VJ_ROMS@/yarc.j64
11810   expect loaded=1
11810   expect core-option=virtualjaguar_internal_resolution:absent
11810   key tap F4
11850   expect menu-open=1
11850   pad tap dpdown
11860   pad tap dpdown
11870   pad tap dpdown
11880   pad tap dpdown
11890   pad tap dpdown
11910   pad tap a
11915   pad tap dpup
11920   pad tap dpup
11925   pad tap dpup
11928   pad tap dpup
11930   pad tap a
11950   pad tap dpdown
11960   pad tap dpdown
11980   pad tap dpright
12000   pad tap b
12020   pad tap b
12040   pad tap b
12080   expect menu-open=0
12080   expect core-option=virtualjaguar_internal_resolution:2x

# "More settings..." opened from the in-game menu keeps the menu underneath and hands the pad to the window only.  Down x5 is Settings,
# A the groups, Down x4 lands on Interface (it clamps there, so the group the screen was left on does not matter), A its rows, Down x6
# clamps on More settings..., A opens the window.  The window's pad presses never reach the menu: two Ups and a shoulder button go to
# it, B closes it, and the menu is where it was -- the focus is still on More settings... (A opens the window again), and it takes
# two more B to leave the Settings screen and one to Resume.  Esc closes the window the same way.
12100   key tap F4
12140   expect menu-open=1
12140   pad tap dpdown
12150   pad tap dpdown
12160   pad tap dpdown
12170   pad tap dpdown
12180   pad tap dpdown
12200   pad tap a
12220   pad tap dpdown
12230   pad tap dpdown
12240   pad tap dpdown
12250   pad tap dpdown
12270   pad tap a
12290   pad tap dpdown
12300   pad tap dpdown
12310   pad tap dpdown
12320   pad tap dpdown
12330   pad tap dpdown
12340   pad tap dpdown
12360   pad tap a
12400   expect settings-open=1
12400   expect tv-more=1
12400   expect menu-open=1
12400   expect paused=1
12400   pad tap dpup
12410   pad tap dpup
12420   pad tap leftshoulder
12460   expect menu-open=1
12460   pad tap b
12500   expect settings-open=0
12500   expect tv-more=0
12500   expect menu-open=1
12500   expect paused=1
12500   pad tap a                  # the focus did not move: More settings... again
12540   expect settings-open=1
12540   expect tv-more=1
12540   key tap Escape
12580  expect settings-open=0
12580  expect tv-more=0
12580  expect menu-open=1
12580  pad tap b                  # rows -> groups
12600  pad tap b                  # groups -> the menu
12640  expect menu-open=1
12640  pad tap b                  # Resume
12680  expect menu-open=0
12680  expect paused=0

# A window that is no longer "live" is never left over a running game (its pad player could not close it, and the pads are the
# game's): a Share hold closes the menu under "More settings..." (the game unpauses and polls its pad itself), and the window goes
# with the hand-off.  Same walk as above to open the window, then the hold.
12720  key tap F4
12760  expect menu-open=1
12760  pad tap dpdown
